{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_51_481997833#9_989623784","relevance":1,"reason":"This Reuters explainer discusses natural gas, methane emissions, CCS technology, and climate disaster. The word technology refers to carbon capture, not electronics or electronic-device use, so it does not answer the information need.","learned":"Queries using broad 'technology' with climate-disaster terms tend to retrieve energy-sector technology rather than consumer electronics."},"action":{"op":"query","query":"(^ (+ \"electronic devices\" electronics smartphones computers) (+ \"environmental problems\" \"environmental impact\" pollution) (+ \"global warming\" \"climate change\"))","reason":"Search for pages dedicated to environmental problems or impacts of electronic devices, which may explicitly explain electronics' role in global warming and climate-related disasters."}}
{"request":{"op":"query","query":"(^ (+ \"electronic devices\" electronics smartphones computers) (+ \"environmental problems\" \"environmental impact\" pollution) (+ \"global warming\" \"climate change\"))"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_27_1269207283#5_2554477208","ok":true,"op":"query","qid":"q2213","rank":1,"snippet":"Computers also contribute to energy waste. Waste creates needless pollution that could be saved each year if businesses and households would shut down their computers and power off their monitors when they are not using them. U.S. businesses waste approximately 1 billion dollars each year in electricity used to power computers and monitors left on after hours. Putting your computer on stand-by or letting your monitor go into sleep mode also creates energy waste, as these modes still require power. Even leaving your computer plugged in while it is shut down will draw a small amount of power from your electrical outlet. This energy waste translates into greenhouse excess gases that contribute to pollution and global <cover>climate change. Production The production of computers creates pollution. </cover>The manufacturing of computers requires a large amount of fossil fuels and chemicals. Despite the fact that computers continue to decrease in size, computers still require 10 times their weight in chemicals and pollutants during manufacturing.\" , \"start_char\": 5038.000000 , \"title\": \"\" , \"url\": \"https://sciencing.com/how-do-computers-pollute-the-environment-13660586.html\" }"}}
{"request":{"judgments":"17/50"}}
{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_27_1269207283#5_2554477208","relevance":2,"reason":"This page is directly about how computers pollute the environment and explains that computer energy waste and manufacturing use fossil fuels/chemicals, creating greenhouse gases that contribute to pollution and global climate change. It strongly supports the electronics-to-climate-change mechanism, but the snippet does not explicitly connect that climate change to natural disasters.","learned":"Computers left on or plugged in waste electricity; that energy waste translates into excess greenhouse gases contributing to global climate change, and computer manufacturing uses fossil fuels and chemicals that create pollution."},"action":{"op":"document","docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_27_1269207283#5_2554477208","reason":"The snippet is highly promising and dedicated to electronics' environmental impacts; inspect the full document to see whether it explicitly links computer-caused climate change or pollution to natural disasters."}}
{"request":{"op":"document","docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_27_1269207283#5_2554477208"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_27_1269207283#5_2554477208","document":"  ... The amount of electricity needed to power computers contributes to the millions of tons of greenhouse gases that are emitted into the atmosphere each year. Energy Waste Computers also contribute to energy waste. Waste creates needless pollution that could be saved each year if businesses and households would shut down their computers and power off their monitors when they are not using them. U.S. businesses waste approximately 1 billion dollars each year in electricity used to power computers and monitors left on after hours. Putting your computer on stand-by or letting your monitor go into sleep mode also creates energy waste, as these modes still require power. Even leaving your computer plugged in while it is shut down will draw a small amount of power from your electrical outlet. This energy waste translates into greenhouse excess gases that contribute to pollution and global climate change. Production The production of computers creates pollution. The manufacturing of computers requires a large amount of fossil fuels and chemicals. Despite the fact that computers continue to decrease in size, computers still require 10 times their weight in chemicals and pollutants during manufacturing.","ok":true,"op":"document"}}
