{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_30_1543580871#10_3275991478","relevance":2,"reason":"The passage gives a clear causal chain: human activities, especially fossil fuels used for electricity, produce greenhouse gases; global warming and climate change then have disastrous consequences including an increased rate of natural disasters. It supports the electricity-use mechanism relevant to electronics, but it is not specifically about electronics or electronic devices.","learned":"Fossil-fuel electricity use is a major human source of greenhouse-gas emissions, and global warming/climate change can increase natural disasters."},"action":{"op":"query","query":"(^ (+ \"electronic gadgets\" electronics \"electronic devices\" computers smartphones) (+ \"carbon footprint\" \"greenhouse gas emissions\" \"energy consumption\") (+ \"climate disaster\" \"natural disasters\" \"extreme weather\"))","reason":"Try alternate wording around electronic gadgets/devices, carbon footprint, energy consumption, and climate-disaster/extreme-weather outcomes to find a document dedicated to the full causal chain."}}
{"request":{"op":"query","query":"(^ (+ \"electronic gadgets\" electronics \"electronic devices\" computers smartphones) (+ \"carbon footprint\" \"greenhouse gas emissions\" \"energy consumption\") (+ \"climate disaster\" \"natural disasters\" \"extreme weather\"))"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_54_312387066#4_714370123","ok":true,"op":"query","qid":"q2231","rank":1,"snippet":"Work/Life Balance The HR Role in Promoting Corporate Social Responsibility Your Employees Respect and Identify with Employers Who Give Implement and Encourage Green Practices Foster a Culture of Corporate Social Responsibility Celebrate Corporate Social Responsibility Successes Three Key Areas of Corporate Social Responsibility Community Relations Training and Development A Cohesive Global Corporate Social Responsibility Platform \" , \"segment\": \"recognize departmental efforts. Collect food, and especially donations, for victims of floods, hurricanes and other <cover>natural disasters around the globe. Encourage reduced energy consumption; subsidize transit passes, make it easy for employees to carpool, encourage staggered staffing to allow after rush hour transit. Permit telecommuting and allow employees working remotely to the degree possible. Encourage shutting off lights, computers, </cover>and printers after work hours and on weekends for further energy reductions. Work with IT to switch to laptops over desktop computers. ( Laptops consume up to 90% less power.) Increase the use of teleconferencing, rather than on-site meetings and trips. Promote brown-bagging in the office to help employees reduce fat and calories to live healthier lives and reduce packaging waste, too.\" , \"start_char\": 2373.000000 , \"title\""}}
