{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_01_1489181295#0_2125111476","relevance":2,"reason":"This page is dedicated to household causes of global warming and directly states that appliances and electronic devices use electricity, much of it from coal/oil, causing greenhouse-gas emissions; using electronics more efficiently can lower consumption. It supports the electronics-to-global-warming link but does not explicitly connect global warming to natural disasters.","learned":"Household appliances and electronic devices cause greenhouse-gas emissions through electricity use, especially when electricity comes from fossil fuels; efficient use reduces emissions."},"action":{"op":"next","qid":"q2234","reason":"The current query is producing substantive pages about electronics/appliances, electricity, greenhouse gases, and global warming; continue to look for results that also include the natural-disaster or extreme-weather consequence."}}
{"request":{"op":"next","qid":"q2234"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_22_18357475#9_46037508","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q2234","rank":3,"snippet":"\": \"Trashed batteries are the biggest source of heavy metal toxins in our landfills, according to the California Energy Commission. Leaving battery-powered appliances and games running when not in use contributes to the risk of heavy metal pollution. One Step at a Time Reduce your home’s carbon footprint one step at a time. A programmable thermostat pays for itself in energy savings within the first year of use. Replacing your incandescent bulbs with compact fluorescent light bulbs can save as much as $40 per bulb in energy usage. Replace worn weather stripping, add insulation and install storm windows to save on climate-control energy costs. Shut down the computer and unplug televisions, lamps and other <cover>appliances when you’re not using them. ‒‒:‒‒ / ‒‒:‒‒ Replay Skip Ads by Read More References U.S. Department of Energy: Energy Storage EPA, Climate Change -- Greenhouse Gas Emissions: In the Home CarbonFund.org:\" , \"start_char\": 5573.000000 , \"title\": \"Reasons Why Wasting Energy </cover>in Homes Is Bad | Home Guides | SF Gate\" , \"url\": \"https://homeguides.sfgate.com/reasons-wasting-energy-homes-bad-78910.html\" }"}}
