{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_48_1263986546#9_2309050602","relevance":1,"reason":"This is the same New York Times roundup item previously seen: it briefly notes California regulations to reduce greenhouse-gas emissions from computer energy use and separately mentions droughts. It is not dedicated to explaining electronics use causing global warming or natural disasters.","learned":"Computer energy-use regulations are linked to greenhouse-gas reductions, but roundup snippets do not provide a focused causal explanation."},"action":{"op":"query","query":"(^ (+ \"wasting electricity\" \"using too much electricity\" \"electricity consumption\") (+ \"global warming\" \"climate change\") (+ \"natural disasters\" \"extreme weather\" hurricanes floods droughts wildfires))","reason":"Look for documents explaining the broader mechanism most relevant to electronics use: electricity consumption or waste contributes to global warming/climate change, which then causes or worsens natural disasters and extreme weather."}}
{"request":{"op":"query","query":"(^ (+ \"wasting electricity\" \"using too much electricity\" \"electricity consumption\") (+ \"global warming\" \"climate change\") (+ \"natural disasters\" \"extreme weather\" hurricanes floods droughts wildfires))"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_53_622938489#1_1304625055","ok":true,"op":"query","qid":"q2236","rank":1,"snippet":"Take advantage of federal and state incentives. 5. The cost of solar is going down. 6. Increase your home’s value. 7. Solar panels offer long-term value. 8. The solar industry is creating jobs. 9. Renewable energy offsets the costs of <cover>climate change. 10. Sunlight costs $0. How much do home solar systems cost? Sunrun Team \" , \"segment\": \"Get a more predictable electric bill. Does it feel like your electricity bill gets higher and higher every year? It’s not just you. Electricity costs have risen by 16% over the past ten years, and this is a trend that’s likely to continue. 1 Factors like extensive repairs to grid infrastructure, rising energy costs, and cranking up the AC or the heat because of increasingly extreme weather all contribute to higher electric bills. 2,3 Several factors can lower your monthly utility bill when you go solar, including overall electricity consumption, </cover>solar energy system size, direct hours of daily sunlight, and the size and angle of your roof. 4 In addition, if you live in a region with especially high electricity rates like the Northeast and the West Coast, you stand to save even "}}
